# Code Style Guide — DNA Music

## TypeScript

* `strict: true` in all tsconfig files.
* Prefer `interface` for public contracts; use `type` for unions and utility types.
* Use named exports in domain modules; default exports only for page-level React components when applicable.
* Use `readonly` for immutable DTO properties.

## Naming Conventions

| Scope               | Convention                                        | Example             |
| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------- |
| Backend files       | kebab-case                                        | `student.service.ts`   |
| Classes             | PascalCase                                        | `StudentService`       |
| Functions/variables | camelCase                                         | `findById`          |
| Constants           | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE                                  | `MAX_FILE_SIZE`     |
| Prisma enums        | PascalCase enum name, SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE values | `StudentStatus.ACTIVE` |
| React components    | PascalCase file name and export                   | `StudentsTable.tsx`    |

## Backend

* One module = one folder under `src/modules/`.
* Controllers: handle HTTP only; delegate logic to services.
* Services: business logic, transactions, and orchestration.
* Repositories: the single access point to Prisma per entity.
* DTOs: Zod schemas + inferred types (`z.infer<typeof schema>`).

## Frontend

* HTTP services only in `src/services/`.
* Server state: hooks in `src/hooks/` or within the corresponding module.
* Presentation vs container components: use clear naming (`UsersTable` vs `UsersPage`).

## Formatting

* Prettier: single quotes, ES5 trailing commas, `printWidth: 100`.
* ESLint: no warnings in CI; `no-explicit-any` set to error.

## Commit Messages (Reference)

* `feat(module): description`
* `fix(module): description`
* `chore: description`
